# Deliberately no catch-all rewrite.
#
# Every route is built as its own file (index.html, photos.html,
# photos/<id>.html), so nothing needs rewriting to boot the app — and sending
# `/* /index.html 200` would answer 200 for every mistyped path, which invites a
# search engine to index an unbounded set of duplicate pages and leaves an agent
# unable to tell a wrong URL from a right one.
#
# Unmatched requests fall through to 404.html, which Cloudflare Pages serves
# with a real 404.

# The blog was retired. Its old addresses send readers home rather than to a
# dead end; feed.xml is left to 404 so feed readers report it plainly.
/blog       /   301
/blog.md    /   301
/blog/*     /   301
